{"id":292019,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-057-004","segment_id":"UT22084-057-004-1531","title":"The Dhāraṇī of the Jewel Torch","raw_text":"The verse passage from down to this point in the text is a close match in terms of content to the entirety of chapter 17 of the Tibetan Avataṃsaka­sūtra, “Bhadraśrī” (chapter 12 of the Chinese), though a different translation in Tibetan. See and .","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/057-004_toh145,847-the_dharani_of_the_jewel_torch.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh145","sequence_no":2123,"relation_ids":["UT22084-057-004-865"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":292020,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-057-004","segment_id":"UT22084-057-004-866","title":"The Dhāraṇī of the Jewel Torch","raw_text":"Then the Blessed One, having taught those verses, remained silent.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/057-004_toh145,847-the_dharani_of_the_jewel_torch.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh145","sequence_no":2124,"relation_ids":["toh145"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":292021,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-057-004","segment_id":"UT22084-057-004-869","title":"The Dhāraṇī of the Jewel Torch","raw_text":"The venerable Subhūti said to the Blessed One, “Blessed One, the appearance of such a jewel of the sūtras in the world is hard to find. Nevertheless, through the power of the Tathāgata such a Dharma has appeared in the world, and solely through the power of the Tathāgata, those sentient beings also heard it.”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/057-004_toh145,847-the_dharani_of_the_jewel_torch.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh145","sequence_no":2127,"relation_ids":["toh145"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":292022,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-057-004","segment_id":"UT22084-057-004-870","title":"The Dhāraṇī of the Jewel Torch","raw_text":"Then the Blessed One, using his speech, said to the venerable Ānanda, “Ānanda, retain this Dharma discourse! Hold it! Seize it! Learn it!”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/057-004_toh145,847-the_dharani_of_the_jewel_torch.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh145","sequence_no":2128,"relation_ids":["toh145"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":292023,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-057-004","segment_id":"UT22084-057-004-872","title":"The Dhāraṇī of the Jewel Torch","raw_text":"Then, after the Blessed One had spoken, that full assembly of bodhisattvas, the bodhisattvas Samanta­bhadra and Mañjuśrī Kumāra­bhūta, and the elder Śāradvatī­putra, the other great śrāvakas, and the world with its gods, humans, asuras, and gandharvas all rejoiced, and they praised what the Blessed One had said.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/057-004_toh145,847-the_dharani_of_the_jewel_torch.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh145","sequence_no":2130,"relation_ids":["toh145"],"export_role":"primary"}
